b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), Boolean arrays (5.2), procedures with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6), conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), a program that reads each stage as it arrives, which counts as the same computation (systems file, The same computation), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation until enough of its places are known, with a list for each unknown of the relations it occurs in and a queue of the unknowns newly given values, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 2: k, of x_j = k. Stage 1 has no constants: its relations are given by the instance's size n and arrival order, from the instance line, order 1 ascending, 2 descending and 3 interleaved;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P16a. Integer unknowns x1 to xn, each a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it. Stage 1: succ(x_i, x_i+1) for i = 1 to n - 1, in the instance's arrival order. Stage 2: x_j = k, where j = ceil(n/2). Each relation is held as posed, and is examined when it arrives and again when one of its places is given a value, never otherwise. succ(a, b) is the relation b = a + 1. Its evaluator gives b the value a + 1 when a is known, or a the value b - 1 when b is known, or tests b = a + 1 when both are, and is then decided, and when neither is known it waits. x_j = k gives x_j the value k, or tests it. For each unknown the program keeps the list of the relations it occurs in, in the order they arrived, and a queue of the unknowns given values and not yet followed. After each relation is posed, the queue is emptied: for each unknown in it, every relation still held on its list is examined, in the order of the list. So a relation is examined at most once for each of its places, and the chain is followed outward from x_j once. Nothing eliminates unknowns between two waiting relations. The store is sized from n;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, order, nu, nrmax;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line. The code that follows n and the cap is the arrival order;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  order := 1;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ code := read; order := code e̲n̲d̲;
  nu := i̲f̲ n < 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ n;
  nrmax := nu + 2;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ nr, nheld, nknown, no, qh, qt, kval, j, w, w2, sx, sw, sd, fx, mostx, u, o, r;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ inconsistent;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ rk, ra, rb, rc, ex[1:nrmax], val, ohd, otl, qu[1:nu], orel, onext[1:2 × nrmax];
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ held[1:nrmax], kn[1:nu];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ occur(u, r);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ u, r; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ u, r;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the relation r is put at the end of the list of unknown u;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    no := no + 1; orel[no] := r; onext[no] := 0;
    i̲f̲ ohd[u] = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ ohd[u] := no e̲l̲s̲e̲ onext[otl[u]] := no;
    otl[u] := no
  e̲n̲d̲ occur;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ give(u, v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ u, v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ u, v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ unknown u is given the value v, and joins the queue;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    val[u] := v; kn[u] := t̲r̲u̲e̲; nknown := nknown + 1;
    qt := qt + 1; qu[qt] := u
  e̲n̲d̲ give;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ decide(r);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ r; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ r;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the relation r is decided, and is held no longer;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ held[r] := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; nheld := nheld - 1 e̲n̲d̲ decide;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine(r);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ r; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ r;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of relation r: kind 1 is succ(a, b), kind 2 is a = c;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b;
    a := ra[r]; b := rb[r];
    ex[r] := ex[r] + 1;
    i̲f̲ rk[r] = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      sx := sx + 1;
      i̲f̲ ex[r] > mostx t̲h̲e̲n̲ mostx := ex[r];
      i̲f̲ kn[a] ∧ kn[b] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sd := sd + 1; i̲f̲ val[b] ≠ val[a] + 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲; decide(r) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ kn[a] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sd := sd + 1; give(b, val[a] + 1); decide(r) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ kn[b] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ sd := sd + 1; give(a, val[b] - 1); decide(r) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ sw := sw + 1
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      fx := fx + 1;
      i̲f̲ kn[a] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ val[a] ≠ rc[r] t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ give(a, rc[r]);
      decide(r)
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the queue is emptied: for each unknown in it, in turn, every relation still held on its list is examined;
  f̲o̲r̲ w := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ qh ≤ qt d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    u := qu[qh]; qh := qh + 1;
    o := ohd[u];
    f̲o̲r̲ w2 := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ o ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      r := orel[o];
      i̲f̲ held[r] t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine(r);
      o := onext[o]
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ pose(kind, a, b, c);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ kind, a, b, c; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ kind, a, b, c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a relation arrives: it is held, put on the lists of its unknowns, examined, and what it gives is followed;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    nr := nr + 1;
    rk[nr] := kind; ra[nr] := a; rb[nr] := b; rc[nr] := c; ex[nr] := 0;
    held[nr] := t̲r̲u̲e̲; nheld := nheld + 1;
    occur(a, nr);
    i̲f̲ kind = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ occur(b, nr);
    examine(nr);
    propagate
  e̲n̲d̲ pose;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ uname(u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ u; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the name of unknown u;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x'); num(u) e̲n̲d̲ uname;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ values;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: every unknown with a value, in order, separated by commas, five to a line;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, c;
    c := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ v := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nu d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ kn[v] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ c > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
        i̲f̲ c > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ c - c ÷ 5 × 5 = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        uname(v); PRINTTEXT(` = '); num(val[v]); c := c + 1
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ values;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: every relation still held, in the order it arrived, separated by commas, five to a line;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, c;
    c := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ h := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nr d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ held[h] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ c > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
        i̲f̲ c > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ c - c ÷ 5 × 5 = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        i̲f̲ rk[h] = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`succ('); uname(ra[h]); PRINTTEXT(`, '); uname(rb[h]); PRINTTEXT(`)') e̲n̲d̲
        e̲l̲s̲e̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ uname(ra[h]); PRINTTEXT(` = '); num(rc[h]) e̲n̲d̲;
        c := c + 1
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ binds;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a bind tag for every unknown with a value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
    f̲o̲r̲ v := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nu d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ kn[v] t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind '); uname(v); PRINTTEXT(`]'); num(val[v]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ binds;

  nr := nheld := nknown := no := sx := sw := sd := fx := mostx := 0;
  qh := 1; qt := 0;
  inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  f̲o̲r̲ u := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nu d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ kn[u] := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; ohd[u] := 0; otl[u] := 0 e̲n̲d̲;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, and the stage it poses;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ stage 1: succ(x_i, x_i+1) for i = 1 to n - 1, in the arrival order;
      i̲f̲ order = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ n - 1 d̲o̲ pose(1, j, j + 1, 0) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ order = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ f̲o̲r̲ j := n - 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ -1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ 1 d̲o̲ pose(1, j, j + 1, 0) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 2 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ n - 1 d̲o̲ pose(1, j, j + 1, 0);
        f̲o̲r̲ j := 2 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 2 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ n - 1 d̲o̲ pose(1, j, j + 1, 0)
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ stage 2: x_j = k, where j = ceil(n/2), with k from the constants;
      kval := read;
      j := (n + 1) ÷ 2;
      pose(2, j, 0, kval)
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: the unknowns with values, and the relations still held;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
      i̲f̲ nknown = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no unknown is known') e̲l̲s̲e̲ values;
      i̲f̲ nheld > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`,'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲; PRINTTEXT(`where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the relations held, the values known, and how often the relations were examined;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`held relations: ');
    i̲f̲ nheld = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
    NLCR;
    binds;
    i̲f̲ nheld > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); num(nheld); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`unknowns known: '); num(nknown); PRINTTEXT(` of '); num(nu); NLCR;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations succ-examined '); num(sx); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations succ-decided '); num(sd); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations succ-waited '); num(sw); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations equation-examined '); num(fx); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`most examinations of one succ relation: '); num(mostx); NLCR;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
